  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Startup Act Burundi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Entrepreneurship is an important mechanism to realize increases in aggregate well-being. For entrepreneurship to flourish do young entrepreneurs need to be able to start their companies. However, start-ups are often held back by challenges in the startup ecosystem. This is also the case in Burundi. Among the challenges identified were the heavy tax burden, lack of certification options, formalization burden, access to finance, legal framework, and access to information and infrastructure, like lack of internet. To counter these challenges, to support start-ups and ultimately and to increase well-being, comprehensive improved entrepreneurship policy will be developed. This project focuses on the development of that improved entrepreneurship policy in Burundi. If implemented well, it can create a massive boost to the startup ecosystem and the Burundian economy at large.</narrative>
  </description>
